  "label": "potential recruits",
  "description": "The meme is designed to target individuals who are considering enlisting in the military, particularly those who are motivated by the prospect of free college education. The visual of disciplined soldiers marching and the text 'we're getting ready to go march for free college' and 'care to join?' directly appeal to this demographic by framing military service as a necessary or recommended path to achieve educational goals. The audience is likely young adults or those seeking educational opportunities, who may be influenced by the promise of tuition coverage or scholarships associated with military enlistment.",
